lines=['# Verified completion and calibration results — 2026-09-07','','All12 fixed trials passed repair and the explicit completion gate. Ten exercised recycling and passed full continuity. The two v2 archive-slicing trials completed all required reads without recycling; conditional recovery was therefore not required. They remain counted as no continuity coverage, not as demonstrated recycling. All four12K long-window trials passed six-file delivery and recovery.','','| Measure | Previous v7 evaluation | Frozen v8 rerun |','| --- | ---: | ---: |','| Correct repairs | 9/12 | 12/12 |','| Recycling continuity | 7/12 | 10/12 |','| Provider failures | 2 | 0 |','| Token reservation failures | 1 | 0 |','| 12K repair plus continuity | 2/4 | 4/4 |','','The [same schedule](fixed-evaluation/manifest.json), task manifests, request hashes, fixture bytes and oracles were verified against the previous run. The candidate changed, so these small non-simultaneous samples are not a controlled causal estimate; absence of provider failures cannot be attributed to the engine change. [Every trial](fixed-evaluation/README.md) remains recorded. No retries or replacements occurred.','','## Implementation','','The opt-in verified-completion-v8 policy validates explicit completion_requirements: required_reads, distinct_turns, archive_after_recycle. Requirements are included in scope binding and cannot change on resume. Before candidate acceptance, the gate checks confirmed full-file delivery, the required distinct read turns and confirmed meaningful archive recovery after any recycle. Deferred, attempted, undelivered or partial reads cannot satisfy a whole-file requirement. Early valid patch submission returns glm.completion-requirements-unmet and no accepted candidate; it never triggers an automatic retry or patch rewriting.','','The CLI and benchmark bind a512-token tokenizer margin for v8. Programmatic clients must match it. The256-token soft-headroom reservation and2048 output reserve remain separate and unchanged. The prompt replaces duplicate per-file progress with a compact gate view; full ledger evidence is retained. Existing policies and defaults retain their behavior. Reports independently check requirement/task bindings and reject accepted candidates with unmet requirements.','','## Calibration','',f"The [prior calibration](calibration.json) used{cal['sample_count']} paired measured responses and excluded two unknown-usage model receipts. Its maximum observed underestimate was{cal['maximum_difference']} tokens. The selection rule adds128 tokens of slack and rounds upward to a128-token boundary, yielding512. [calibrate.py](calibrate.py) reproduces the calculation without provider calls.",f"The frozen rerun supplied{len(diffs)} measured responses; the maximum difference was{max(diffs)} tokens, within512. This remains empirical calibration, not a universal bound; the runtime underestimate check remains enabled.",'','## Validation and limits','',f"All379 local tests passed ([log](tests.tap)), including early rejection, confirmed recovery acceptance, missing recovery rejection, scope drift on resume, requirement validation and margin binding. The12 live arms used{s['model_attempts']} model and{s['tokenizer_attempts']} tokenizer attempts. Minimum measured soft headroom was{s['minimum_headroom']} tokens. Per-arm caps remained12/24 attempts and580 seconds.",'','Source hashes matched before/after each arm and at aggregation; calibration evidence hashes and unchanged task identities were checked ([validation](validation.json)). Oracle checks ran in isolated copies. Recorded reports verify bindings and receipts, not cryptographic authenticity or a fresh oracle replay. Complete private inputs remain under /tmp/are-glm-completion-fixed-evaluation; exported traces omit raw message history and provider reasoning and are not complete report inputs.','','This verifies ARE admission and observable recovery, not absence of provider-internal compaction. No default activation, publication or deployment occurred. The [construction plan](PLAN.md) preserves D65 scope and operational residue.','','## Open Questions','','- Does512 cover other languages, tool schemas and substantially longer requests?','- How stable are these outcomes across larger independent samples and provider conditions?','- Should workloads that never recycle be tested separately from forced continuity workloads?','- What evidence would justify default activation?','']
(p/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in summary.items() if k!='trials'},indent=2))
